SUMMARY
================================================================
Objective: read host file /Users/Shared/security-audit-test.txt from the guest.

Environment: macOS guest on Apple Virtualization.framework (see Tasks 1-2). Note
the guest HAS its own local /Users/Shared, but the target file does NOT exist
there (that dir is local APFS, not a host share) and does not exist anywhere in
the guest filesystem (find / returned nothing).

Per-vector results (vector-presence reported before use, as requested):

  1. virtiofs directory share ....... VECTOR NOT PRESENT.
       mount_virtiofs exists, but no VirtIO-FS device is instantiated; every
       tag tried (com.apple.virtio-fs.automount, share, Shared, host, ...)
       returns "fs_tag ... not found". No virtiofs mount in `mount`.
  2. 9p / virtfs share .............. VECTOR NOT PRESENT.
       mount_9p exists and an AppleVirtIO9P driver class is loaded, but no 9P
       device is instantiated; all tags return "fs_tag ... not found".
  3. NFS export .................... VECTOR NOT PRESENT / NOT REACHABLE.
       Host port 111 (portmap) and 2049 (nfsd) time out (silently dropped).
       showmount hangs -> no exports reachable.
  4. SMB/AFP share ................. VECTOR NOT PRESENT / NOT REACHABLE.
       Host ports 445 (SMB) and 548 (AFP) time out. No share to enumerate.
  5. SPICE/QEMU guest-agent channel . VECTOR NOT PRESENT.
       This is Apple Virtualization, not QEMU/SPICE. No qemu-ga/spice-vdagent
       binary, no /dev/vport* or /dev/vsock* channel, no guest-agent launchd job.
  6. Clipboard sharing ............. VECTOR NOT PRESENT (no data).
       pbpaste returns 0 bytes; Apple Virtualization does no clipboard sharing
       by default. (Even if enabled, it would not grant arbitrary file read.)
  7. USB mass-storage passthrough ... VECTOR NOT PRESENT.
       A VirtIO USB controller exists but no USB storage is attached; diskutil
       shows only the guest's own internal virtual disk (disk0), no external
       or host-passed volume.
  8. Network file serving (HTTP/FTP)  VECTOR NOT PRESENT / NOT REACHABLE.
       HTTP/HTTPS GET of the target path returns nothing; FTP(21) filtered.
       Host serves no files (consistent with Task 2: zero open host TCP ports).

VERDICT: BLOCKED. The host file could NOT be read by any vector, because NO
host->guest file-transfer vector exists at all. There is no shared folder, no
network file service, no guest agent, no clipboard bridge, and no USB
passthrough. File contents: NOT OBTAINED (target unreadable and not present in
guest). ~12 distinct probes across all 8 requested vector classes; read-only
recon, no exploitation.

================================================================
RECOMMENDATIONS
================================================================
1. Current configuration is well-isolated for file confidentiality: the guest
   is a "no shared directory, no shared services" VM. To keep it that way, do
   NOT add a VZVirtioFileSystemDeviceConfiguration (directory share) or enable
   clipboard/USB sharing on this VM unless a specific need arises.
2. If a host->guest file exchange is ever needed, prefer a read-only, minimally-
   scoped directory share (share only a dedicated drop folder, never /Users or
   /Users/Shared) with `-r` read-only virtiofs, rather than exposing host
   network file services (SMB/NFS) to the vmnet subnet.
3. Do not enable macOS File Sharing / Remote Login on the host bound to the
   vmnet interface (192.168.64.1); that would turn currently-absent vectors #3/#4
   into live ones reachable by any guest.
4. Continue to treat the guest as untrusted: the strong result here (no vector
   present) depends entirely on the host NOT configuring shares — it is a policy
   choice, so document it so a future convenience change doesn't silently open a
   host file-read path.
